Biggest Threats to Online Privacy

Biggest threats to online privacy come from both governments and big company.

Tech giants, data brokers and shady firms scrape users information from the internet and create detailed profile about internet users.

And these are sold to people who want to target or influence internet users towards some certain political positions or lifestyle choices.

Governments can also access this data, which becomes part of a broader survelliance system which nowadays is almost impossible to escape from.

All internet users actions are tracked, it can make it harder to protest or dissent without fear of repercussions.

We need to change the way we think about privacy and fight to protect it.

Today we might feel we have nothing to hide but tommorow upcoming generations might have nowhere to hide.
